        10["<div style='font-weight: bold'>ata::Device</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: ata_device.cpp, identify.cpp]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The hard disk: task file,<br />status, IDENTIFY (patched<br />live when DMA is added),<br />READ/WRITE SECTORS, MULTIPLE<br />and DMA, read-ahead,<br />write-behind, two units.</div>"]
        style 10 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        11["<div style='font-weight: bold'>ATAPI CD-ROM</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: atapi_device.cpp, mmc.cpp, hdcd_device.cpp]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>PACKET commands, MMC<br />(READ(10), TOC, GET EVENT),<br />disc changes; hdcd::Device<br />puts it beside the hard disk.</div>"]
        style 11 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        12["<div style='font-weight: bold'>busAutoStep</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: main.cpp (CORE1_RAM_RARE)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>bus = auto on core 1: applies<br />the DMA patch between<br />commands and switches the<br />program at a quiet moment or<br />while RESET# is held.</div>"]
        style 12 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        13["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Trace ring</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: spsc_ring.h, access_log]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Commands, completions and (on<br />request) every bus access,<br />recorded for core 0 to print.<br />Lock-free SPSC ring.</div>"]
        style 13 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        14["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Fetch mailbox</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: fetch_mailbox.h]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The handshake between the<br />cores: core 1 posts a fetch<br />(LBA, buffer, read or write),<br />core 0 posts the result.<br />Shared memory.</div>"]
        style 14 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        7["<div style='font-weight: bold'>ide_bus</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: ide_bus.cpp]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Loads and serves the bus<br />program: ide_bus, early<br />answers, the data lane,<br />ide_bus_noiordy. Switches<br />early answers <-> the lane<br />live (bus = auto), holds<br />IORDY while core 1 answers,<br />drives INTRQ. The data lane<br />streams data-in words by DMA,<br />without core 1.</div>"]
        style 7 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        8["<div style='font-weight: bold'>ide_table</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: ide_table.cpp, ide_table_write.cpp]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The register table: every<br />register read answered by the<br />PIO from values core 1 keeps<br />ready, for hosts that ignore<br />IORDY.</div>"]
        style 8 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        9["<div style='font-weight: bold'>ide_dma</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: ide_dma.cpp]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Multiword DMA's data phase:<br />hands DD0-15 to its PIO block<br />for a burst, feeds it by a<br />DMA channel, drives DMARQ.</div>"]
        style 9 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
      end

      15["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Core 0: services</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: C++ (Arduino-Pico)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Everything slow: the card,<br />USB serial, the activity<br />link, the diagnostics'<br />reports, the bus = auto<br />advice. Keeps up with core<br />1's fetches before anything<br />else.</div>"]
      style 15 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      25["<div style='font-weight: bold'>PIO programs</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: RP2350 PIO assembly (src/*.pio)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>State machines that meet the<br />IDE bus's nanosecond timing:<br />sample every access, pull<br />IORDY low within 35 ns, drive<br />DD for reads, move DMA data.<br />Three blocks of 32<br />instructions.</div>"]
      style 25 fill:#2e7d5b,stroke:#20573f,color:#ffffff
